msgid "Coverage"
msgstr "Couverture"

msgid ""
"**Coverage** answers the question: *how much of a nested dictionary does "
"a given set of paths describe?*"
msgstr ""
"La **couverture** répond à la question : *quelle part d'un dictionnaire "
"imbriqué un ensemble de chemins donné décrit-il ?*"

msgid ""
"This is useful when you work with a partial or independently defined "
":class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` and want to know how much of a "
"target dictionary it accounts for."
msgstr ""
"C'est utile lorsque vous travaillez avec une "
":class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` partielle ou définie "
"indépendamment, et que vous voulez savoir quelle part d'un dictionnaire "
"cible elle décrit."

msgid ""
"All coverage methods compare two sets of paths: the paths expanded from "
"the compact structure, written *S* below, and the paths of the "
"dictionary, written *T*."
msgstr ""
"Toutes les méthodes de couverture comparent deux ensembles de chemins : "
"les chemins développés à partir de la structure compacte, notés *S* ci-"
"dessous, et les chemins du dictionnaire, notés *T*."

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.coverage` returns the share of *T* "
"found in *S*: the number of paths in both sets divided by the number of "
"paths in *T*. Paths of *S* that are not in *T* do not change it, so the "
"value is always between 0.0 and 1.0."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.coverage` renvoie la part de *T* "
"présente dans *S* : le nombre de chemins communs aux deux ensembles, "
"divisé par le nombre de chemins de *T*. Les chemins de *S* absents de *T*"
" ne la modifient pas ; la valeur est donc toujours comprise entre 0.0 et "
"1.0."

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.is_covering` returns ``True`` when "
"the two sets are equal."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.is_covering` renvoie ``True`` "
"lorsque les deux ensembles sont égaux."

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.uncovered_paths` lists the paths of "
"*T* that are not in *S*."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.uncovered_paths` énumère les chemins"
" de *T* absents de *S*."

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.missing_paths` lists the paths of "
"*S* that are not in *T*."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.missing_paths` énumère les chemins "
"de *S* absents de *T*."

msgid ""
"``coverage() == 1.0`` therefore means that every path of the dictionary "
"is described, while ``is_covering()`` also requires that the structure "
"describes no other path."
msgstr ""
"``coverage() == 1.0`` signifie donc que chaque chemin du dictionnaire est"
" décrit, tandis que ``is_covering()`` exige en plus que la structure ne "
"décrive aucun autre chemin."

msgid "Full coverage"
msgstr "Couverture complète"

msgid ""
"A :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` built directly from a dictionary"
" always covers it completely:"
msgstr ""
"Une :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView` construite directement à "
"partir d'un dictionnaire le couvre toujours entièrement :"

msgid "Partial coverage"
msgstr "Couverture partielle"

msgid "Assign a reduced structure to simulate partial coverage:"
msgstr "Affectez une structure réduite pour simuler une couverture partielle :"

msgid "Identifying uncovered paths"
msgstr "Repérer les chemins non couverts"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.uncovered_paths` returns the paths "
"that exist in the dictionary but are absent from the compact structure:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.uncovered_paths` renvoie les chemins"
" présents dans le dictionnaire mais absents de la structure compacte :"

msgid "Identifying missing paths"
msgstr "Repérer les chemins manquants"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.missing_paths` returns the paths "
"present in the compact structure but absent from the dictionary — useful "
"when the structure was set manually and may contain invalid entries:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.missing_paths` renvoie les chemins "
"présents dans la structure compacte mais absents du dictionnaire, ce qui "
"est utile lorsque la structure a été définie à la main et peut contenir "
"des entrées invalides :"

msgid "Extra paths"
msgstr "Chemins en trop"

msgid ""
"A structure that describes every path of the dictionary and more has full"
" coverage, but it is not covering, since the two sets of paths differ:"
msgstr ""
"Une structure qui décrit tous les chemins du dictionnaire, et d'autres "
"encore, a une couverture complète, mais elle n'est pas couvrante, puisque"
" les deux ensembles de chemins diffèrent :"

